{"signature": "{\"model\": \"eleven_multilingual_v2\", \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\", \"settings\": {\"similarity_boost\": 0.85, \"stability\": 0.5, \"style\": 0.0, \"use_speaker_boost\": true}, \"text\": \"Energy cannot be created or destroyed. It can be transferred between stores by mechanical work, electrical work, heating or radiation. In a closed system, no energy is transferred into or out of the system, so the total energy remains constant. Be careful: in thermodynamics, a closed system may exchange energy but not matter with its surroundings. For GCSE energy-conservation questions, the important condition is that no energy crosses the boundary of the system when we claim its total energy stays constant; this is more precisely an isolated system.\", \"voice\": \"28e9d9dcea90e5b4\"}", "duration": 38.112653, "words": [["Energy", 0.0], ["cannot", 0.476], ["be", 0.859], ["created", 1.01], ["or", 1.625], ["destroyed.", 1.811], ["It", 2.496], ["can", 2.694], ["be", 2.891], ["transferred", 3.03], ["between", 3.669], ["stores", 4.075], ["by", 4.632], ["mechanical", 4.853], ["work,", 5.492], ["electrical", 6.014], ["work,", 6.687], ["heating", 7.163], ["or", 7.697], ["radiation.", 7.93], ["In", 8.707], ["a", 8.94], ["closed", 9.056], ["system,", 9.427], ["no", 10.066], ["energy", 10.368], ["is", 10.786], ["transferred", 10.913], ["into", 11.575], ["or", 12.144], ["out", 12.399], ["of", 12.748], ["the", 12.992], ["system,", 13.131], ["so", 13.804], ["the", 14.095], ["total", 14.245], ["energy", 14.687], ["remains", 15.255], ["constant.", 15.801], ["Be", 16.59], ["careful:", 16.788], ["in", 17.484], ["thermodynamics,", 17.693], ["a", 18.785], ["closed", 18.97], ["system", 19.353], ["may", 19.876], ["exchange", 20.108], ["energy", 20.642], ["but", 21.199], ["not", 21.455], ["matter", 21.745], ["with", 22.186], ["its", 22.407], ["surroundings.", 22.569], ["For", 23.963], ["GCSE", 24.195], ["energy-conservation", 25.17], ["questions,", 26.354], ["the", 27.051], ["important"